  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, the Joint Trade Union Coordination Centre (JTUCC) improved its connectivity with the member organisations through digitalization of its communication system. There has been a wider participation of union members in the online programmes and meetings by the member organizations because of the improved connectivity.  

JTUCC has also set up Workers Information and Support Centres (WISC) to strengthen institutional capacity of the trade unions throughout the country. This is a model based on experiences from India and is expected to increase trade union membership especially in the informal economy.	

JTUCC has used findings of studies commissioned on the impact of COVID 19 on workers&apos; health and safety, the impact of COVID 19 on migrant workers, and the role of trade unions,  to draw the attention of the Government and employers and relevant authorities, to protect the workers, to provide necessary relief packages to day-workers in the  informal economy, paid leave and other necessary facilities to workers in the formal economy, as well as to provide necessary support to migrant workers.

JTUCC has requested all National Trade Union Centres to sensitize workers and lobby with the provincial and local government for necessary action. Likewise, JTUCC Provincial Committees have been lobbying with the provincial government and employers to provide the necessary protection and facilities to the workers affected by the COVID-19 pandemic. At the request of the JTUCC, ILO provided technical and financial support to strengthen the digital communication system with a view to strengthen connectivity with its member organization. 

ILO extended technical support to commission two studies to prepare background papers on the impact of COVID 19 on workers&apos; health and safety, the impact of COVID 19 on migrant workers, and the role of trade unions.  The ILO facilitated a series of discussions organised by JTUCC on these issues.

With a view to enhance trade unions&apos; engagement in the planning and implementation of SDGs at the country level, the ILO will extent its technical support to the trade unions to strengthen its capacity to influence the national policies and programmes associated to SDGs.    

ILO extended its technical support to JTUCC in developing and finalizing the JTUCC Strategic Plan.</narrative>
   </description>
